  "title": "Arcus Dolabellae et Silani",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/arch"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The consuls P. Cornelius Dolabella and C. Iulius Silanus erected the arch in A.D. 10 (<em>CIL</em> vi. 1384). Built of travertine, it may have supported a branch of the <em>Aqua Marcia</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Situated on the Caelian Hill, the Arcus Dolabellae et Silani sits at the northern corner of the Castra Peregrina. The gate dates to A.D. 10 and is likely a rebuilding of an earlier gate that was part of the so-called Servian Wall, perhaps the Porta Querquetulana (or Querquetularia) or the Porta Caelimontana.",
  "reprPoint": [
